P2 (issue #23, U1): recount the item frequencies of every surrogate.

The miners take the item frequencies from the cache of the transaction
bag (tbg_ifrqs(bag, 0)). Only reading, recoding, filtering and reducing
invalidate it, and fpg_data(FPG_SURR) does none of these, so every
surrogate after the first was mined with the first one's frequencies
(wrong singleton supports, elimination and perfect extensions). For the
fpgrowth program the bag is mined once and the recount changes nothing.
Must be combined with P2b. docs/differences.md row U1.

--- a/fpgrowth/src/fpgrowth.c
+++ b/fpgrowth/src/fpgrowth.c
@@ -745,7 +745,7 @@
   n = tbg_cnt(fpg->tabag);      /* get the number of transactions */
   k = tbg_itemcnt(fpg->tabag);  /* and check the number of items */
   if (k <= 0) return isr_report(fpg->report);
-  f = tbg_ifrqs(fpg->tabag, 0); /* get the item frequencies */
+  f = tbg_ifrqs(fpg->tabag, 1); /* get the item frequencies */
   if (!f) return -1;            /* in the transaction bag */
   s = fpg->set = (ITEM*)malloc((size_t)(k+k) *sizeof(ITEM)
                               +(size_t) k    *sizeof(SUPP));
